# Everything outside the course tree that changes when the installer REFUSES an unsupported
# distribution. This is the shortest expected set in this directory, and that is the claim.
#
#   /work   the read-only mount this harness adds, not the installer
#   C /etc  podman bind-mounts hosts/hostname/resolv.conf into every container, which moves the
#           directory's mtime. Present in every case here.
#
# NOTHING ELSE AT ALL -- and compare that with expected-system-paths.podman-old and
# expected-system-paths.debian, which both carry /tmp runtime directories and (on podman 5.x) a
# ~/.config, all created by the single `podman --version` their survey runs. This refusal never
# reaches that probe: distro_family() returns `unsupported`, survey says so at "Looking at your
# computer" and exits, so podman is never executed and no runtime state is created.
#
# THAT ORDERING IS THE POINT, not a coincidence. A machine this script cannot support should be
# told before it is asked for permission and before anything is inspected on its behalf, which is
# the same order say_intel_mac refuses an Intel Mac in. If a future change moved the refusal later
# -- into install_podman, say -- this file would grow podman's runtime directories and say so.
A /work
C /etc
